ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20553, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WtMPXWzZdao4ERxRoXXXRn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20553, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017jWG7sdibE2qTxEiJES5Fe", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20853, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017jWG7sdibE2qTxEiJES5Fe", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20853, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017jWG7sdibE2qTxEiJES5Fe", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25658, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0129WtntEm9wAMNT2K8skvsh", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A retry finished the rollout. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and error rate is 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into why it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging result, and investigate the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56258, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0129WtntEm9wAMNT2K8skvsh", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56258, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0129WtntEm9wAMNT2K8skvsh", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57863, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GP9RK3vAcyuXqUQUjyPRs4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58163, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GP9RK3vAcyuXqUQUjyPRs4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58163, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GP9RK3vAcyuXqUQUjyPRs4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63267, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt only partly worked. An orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, so us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Rolling to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's only one. Its summary covers the cause, the rollback (including the partial failure) and the current status.\n- **Follow-ups listed in the incident:**\n  - Find what broke in v2.3.1.\n  - Find out why it went to production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012DNU5jqqyLoqfDuEr6BuHx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SGag7XS9NCgi6ZKhbUUF9t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016AijG2Y3WXVSqSKLdkSbcB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013oR19egQmv5bagCdVdWedu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east got rolled back. Rolling to a set version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more to finish the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VP87khya72N56s12otMDX6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WtMPXWzZdao4ERxRoXXXRn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017jWG7sdibE2qTxEiJES5Fe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0129WtntEm9wAMNT2K8skvsh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A retry finished the rollout. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and error rate is 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into why it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging result, and investigate the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GP9RK3vAcyuXqUQUjyPRs4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt only partly worked. An orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, so us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Rolling to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's only one. Its summary covers the cause, the rollback (including the partial failure) and the current status.\n- **Follow-ups listed in the incident:**\n  - Find what broke in v2.3.1.\n  - Find out why it went to production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}